# Performance Plan: Server-Side Data Fetching

## Problem
All pages use `"use client"` with `useEffect` for data fetching, causing:
- Blank screen → spinner → content (poor UX)
- No SEO benefits (content not in initial HTML)
- Waterfall requests (auth check → data fetch → render)

## Solution
Convert key pages to Server Components with server-side data fetching. Interactive parts become separate client components. Create server-compatible query functions.

## Key Insight
Existing query functions use the browser client (`createClient` from `client.ts`) which won't work in Server Components. We need to create `.server.ts` versions that accept a Supabase client parameter.

---

## Files to Create

### Server Query Functions
- `src/lib/supabase/queries/guides.server.ts` - `fetchGuidesServer(supabase, sort, search)`
- `src/lib/supabase/queries/guide-detail.server.ts` - `fetchGuideByIdServer`, `fetchGuideCommentsServer`, `fetchRecommendedGuidesServer`
- `src/lib/supabase/queries/profile.server.ts` - `fetchProfileByUsernameServer`, `fetchUserGuidesServer`

### Client Components (extract interactivity)
- `src/components/gallery/sort-tabs-server.tsx` - URL-based sort tabs using `<Link>`
- `src/components/guide/guide-detail-client.tsx` - Handles like/save/follow status + interactions
- `src/components/profile/profile-page-client.tsx` - Tab switching + lazy loading

### Loading/Error States
- `src/app/loading.tsx`
- `src/app/guide/[guideId]/[slug]/loading.tsx`
- `src/app/guide/[guideId]/[slug]/not-found.tsx`
- `src/app/profile/[username]/loading.tsx`
- `src/app/profile/[username]/not-found.tsx`

---

## Files to Modify

### 1. Home Page (`src/app/page.tsx`)

Remove `"use client"`, convert to async Server Component:
```typescript
import { createClient } from "@/lib/supabase/server";
import { fetchGuidesServer } from "@/lib/supabase/queries/guides.server";

export default async function Home({ searchParams }) {
  const { q: query, sort = "trending" } = await searchParams;
  const supabase = await createClient();
  const guides = await fetchGuidesServer(supabase, sort, query);

  return (
    <div>
      <SortTabsServer active={sort} query={query} />
      <GuideGrid guides={guides} />
    </div>
  );
}
```

Sort changes use URL navigation (`?sort=recent`) for full SSR benefits.

### 2. Guide Detail (`src/app/guide/[guideId]/[slug]/page.tsx`)

Remove `"use client"`, fetch data server-side, pass to client wrapper:
```typescript
export default async function GuideDetailPage({ params }) {
  const { guideId } = await params;
  const supabase = await createClient();

  const guide = await fetchGuideByIdServer(supabase, guideId);
  if (!guide) notFound();

  const [comments, recommended] = await Promise.all([
    fetchGuideCommentsServer(supabase, guideId),
    fetchRecommendedGuidesServer(supabase, guideId, guide.category_id),
  ]);

  const { data: { user } } = await supabase.auth.getUser();

  return (
    <GuideDetailClient
      guide={guide}
      initialComments={comments}
      recommended={recommended}
      user={user}
    />
  );
}
```

User-specific status checks (like/save/follow) remain client-side in `GuideDetailClient`.

### 3. Profile Page (`src/app/profile/[username]/page.tsx`)

Remove `"use client"`, fetch profile + initial guides server-side:
```typescript
export default async function ProfilePage({ params }) {
  const { username } = await params;
  const supabase = await createClient();

  const profile = await fetchProfileByUsernameServer(supabase, username);
  if (!profile) notFound();

  const { data: { user } } = await supabase.auth.getUser();
  const initialGuides = await fetchUserGuidesServer(supabase, profile.id);

  return (
    <ProfilePageClient
      profile={profile}
      currentUserId={user?.id ?? null}
      isOwner={!!user && user.id === profile.id}
      initialGuides={initialGuides}
    />
  );
}
```

Tab switching and lazy-loading of comments/liked/saved tabs remain client-side.

---

## Verification

1. `npm run build` - should complete without errors
2. `npm run dev` and test:
   - Home page: guides visible immediately, no spinner flash
   - Guide detail: content renders on initial load
   - Profile: profile + guides tab visible immediately
   - View page source (Ctrl+U): HTML contains actual guide titles/content
3. Network tab: initial page load includes data in HTML, no separate fetch waterfall

